      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on our auth-service microservice in our GKE cluster. i've checked the basic logs but they're pretty sparse. can u give me a diagnostic checklist to figure out if this is a resource limit issue, a liveness/readiness probe failure, or just a bad config? \n\nhere's the snippet from the pod events:\nEvents:\n  Type     Reason     Age                From               Message\n  ----     ------     ----               ----               -------\n  Normal   Scheduled  15m                default-scheduler  Successfully assigned default/auth-service-7f8d to node-1\n  Normal   Pulling    14m                kubelet            Pulling image \"gcr.io/prod-cluster/auth-service:v2.1.4\"\n  Normal   Pulled     14m                kubelet            Successfully pulled image \"gcr.io/prod-cluster/auth-service:v2.1.4\"\n  Normal   Created    14m                kubelet            Created container auth-service\n  Normal   Started    14m                kubelet            Started container auth-service\n  Warning  BackOff    2m (x5 over 10m)   kubelet            Back-off restarting failed container",
